    story:"Interlaken sits on the narrow strip of land between Lake Thun and Lake Brienz — 'inter lacus' is Latin for 'between the lakes.' Stand in the Höhematte meadow in the town centre and look south: the Eiger (3,967m), Mönch (4,107m), and Jungfrau (4,158m) are directly in front of you, completely filling the horizon. The Eiger's North Face — one of the most feared climbs in the Alps — is visible on the left. 64 people died attempting the first ascent of the Eiger North Face before it was finally climbed in 1938.",
    history:"First mentioned in records as a monastery in 1133. The town became a major stop on the Victorian Grand Tour after Thomas Cook organized the first package tour here in 1863. The Jungfrau Railway (to the highest railway station in Europe, 3,454m) was completed in 1912 after 16 years of construction.",
    itinerary:[
      {time:"17:30",icon:"🏠",title:"Check in Airbnb",desc:"From Lauterbrunnen train, arrive Interlaken Ost, walk or short taxi to your Airbnb near Interlaken West.",tip:"Ask your Airbnb host in advance if you can do an early bag drop at 12:15 when you first arrive in Interlaken before going to Lauterbrunnen. Many hosts accommodate this."},
      {time:"18:00",icon:"🏔",title:"Höhematte meadow — Eiger view",desc:"5 min walk from your Airbnb. A large public meadow in the centre of town. Look south. The Eiger, Mönch, and Jungfrau are directly in front of you. On clear evenings the peaks turn pink-orange (Alpenglow). This is free. This is the most famous mountain view in Switzerland.",tip:"The Alpenglow (when the peaks turn pink) happens about 30 minutes after sunset. June sunset is around 21:15 — so Alpenglow is around 21:45. Worth waiting for."},
      {time:"19:00",icon:"🍽",title:"Dinner + early sleep",desc:"Migros supermarket for supplies (cheapest in Switzerland), or any restaurant on Höheweg. Early sleep — 07:30 departure tomorrow for Zürich and Imst.",tip:"Migros and Coop are the Swiss supermarket chains. CHF 8–12 for a full meal from the Migros restaurant counter. Swiss eating out is expensive — supermarket is the smart choice."},
      {time:"07:30",icon:"🚄",title:"Direct train → Zürich via Bern",desc:"2 hours. No change. Direct SBB train to Zürich HB via Bern. Arrive Zürich 09:30. 5 full hours in Zürich.",tip:"The departure is from Interlaken West station (not Ost). Check which platform at Interlaken West the evening before."},
    ],
