    tagline:"Mozart was born here. Schafbergbahn 1,783m. Hallstatt UNESCO village day-trip.",
    color:"#E65100", bg:"#FFF8F0", currency:"EUR", budget:"€65–90/night",
    budgetBreakdown: { accommodation: 80, food: 28, transport: 12, activities: 25, misc: 8, currency: "EUR", days: 2, note: "Schafbergbahn €48, Festung €18, Hallstatt day-trip €30, Mozart birthplace €12" },
    story:"Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was born at Getreidegasse 9 on 27 January 1756. He composed his first piece at age 5 and had performed before the Habsburg court by age 6. He died in Vienna aged 35 and was buried in an unmarked pauper's grave — at his own request. The Schafbergbahn steam cogwheel railway has been running since 1893, using some of the oldest working steam locomotives in the world. At the summit (1,783m), you can see 11 lakes simultaneously. The Sound of Music was filmed in Mirabell Gardens, in the fountain, on these steps, on this mountain.",
    history:"Roman settlement Iuvavum from 15 BC. Seat of the Archbishop of Salzburg for 1,200 years — they ruled as princes with their own army. Mozart born here 1756, lived here until age 25. Old City UNESCO World Heritage since 1997. The Salzburg Festival (opera, theatre) has run every August since 1920, bringing 200,000 visitors annually.",
    itinerary:[
      {time:"Mon 22 Jun · 15:00",icon:"🚉",title:"Arrive Salzburg — evening walk",desc:"Check in Schallmoos (10 min walk from Hbf or Bus 1/3/5, €2.60). Walk to the Salzach river. The Hohensalzburg Fortress is lit at night, reflected in the river. This evening walk is free and one of the most beautiful things in Austria.",tip:"The riverside walk from the Staatsbrücke bridge looking up at the fortress at night is the quintessential Salzburg moment. Takes 30 minutes."},
      {time:"Tue 23 Jun · 07:30",icon:"🚌",title:"⭐⭐ SCHAFBERGBAHN DAY — Bus 150 departs",desc:"Bus 150 from Salzburg Hbf Bussteig (Bus Stop) 6 or nearby → St. Gilgen (1hr, €5pp, runs every hour, no booking needed). Buy bus ticket on the bus with card.",tip:"Bus 150 direction 'Bad Ischl'. Get off at St. Gilgen Schiffstation (ferry dock). Journey is 1 hour through beautiful alpine countryside."},
      {time:"08:30",icon:"⛵",title:"Wolfgangsee ferry St. Gilgen → St. Wolfgang",desc:"30 min crossing of a turquoise Alpine lake. €8pp one way. The ferry docks directly at the Schafbergbahn valley station — you walk off the boat and the train is 50 metres away. The lake approach to the mountain is part of the experience.",tip:"Buy a combined ticket if available (ferry + Schafbergbahn) — sometimes offered at the ferry dock. Otherwise buy ferry at the dock and Schafbergbahn at the valley station."},
      {time:"09:20",icon:"🚞",title:"Schafbergbahn first steam cogwheel up",desc:"Book at 5schaetze.at — €42–48pp return. Steam locomotive from 1893. Wooden carriages. 35 minutes to climb 1,190 vertical metres at 26% maximum gradient. The views open progressively — first Wolfgangsee, then Mondsee, then more lakes until at the summit you can see 11 lakes simultaneously. Book the 09:20 departure.",tip:"When buying your ticket, also select your RETURN time — you must choose when you want to come back. 11:30 or 12:00 return allows time for Salzburg city afternoon."},
      {time:"10:00",icon:"🏔",title:"Summit 1,783m — 11 lakes visible",desc:"Hotel Schafbergspitze at the summit has a terrace café with the most extraordinary panoramic view in Austria. Coffee and cake here at 1,783m. You can see Wolfgangsee, Mondsee, Irrsee, Fuschlsee, Attersee, and 6 more lakes on a clear day. Walk the summit ridge (15 min).",tip:"The clouds come in from the west — if there are clouds building on your ascent, you may get a gap between them at the summit. Patience pays."},
      {time:"11:30",icon:"🚞",title:"Steam train back down + ferry",desc:"Pre-booked return descent. The ride down is equally dramatic — steep gradients, mountain views, the lake appearing below. Ferry back to St. Gilgen, Bus 150 to Salzburg. Arrive ~14:00.",tip:"On the descent, the train makes very sharp curves. Sit on the valley side for better views going down (opposite side from the ascent view)."},
      {time:"14:30",icon:"🏰",title:"Hohensalzburg Fortress + Mirabell",desc:"Funicular €12 return up to the fortress (or free 30 min hike). Best panoramic views of the city. Then Mirabell Gardens (completely free) — Do-Re-Mi Sound of Music steps, formal baroque garden.",tip:"The hike up to the fortress through the Altstadt lanes is actually enjoyable and shows you the medieval city. But if you're tired from Schafbergbahn, the funicular is worth the €12."},
      {time:"Wed 24 Jun · 08:30",icon:"🚂",title:"⭐ HALLSTATT day-trip — UNESCO lakeside village",desc:"ÖBB train from Salzburg Hbf → Attnang-Puchheim (50 min) → change → Hallstatt station (50 min, runs along the Hallstättersee). Total 2hrs each way, ~€30pp roundtrip. At Hallstatt station, walk down to the ferry pier — 5 min ferry across the lake (€3.20) drops you in the village itself. The most photographed Alpine village in Austria — pastel houses stacked on a cliff face above a turquoise lake.",tip:"Train tickets: oebb.at, no advance booking needed. Sit on the LEFT side leaving Salzburg for Wolfgangsee views. The classic 'Hallstatt photo' is from the north end of the village square — go early before tour buses arrive (~10:00)."},
      {time:"Wed 24 Jun · 12:00",icon:"⛪",title:"Hallstatt village + bone chapel + salt mine",desc:"Walk Marktplatz (the main square), the wooden boardwalk along the lake. The Beinhaus (bone chapel, €2) at St. Michael's holds 1,200 painted skulls — a Hallstatt tradition since the 12th century when the cemetery ran out of space. Optional: Salzbergbahn funicular (€20pp) to the salt mines and Skywalk viewpoint. Lunch at Gasthof Zauner (lake trout €18) or simpler at the bakery on Marktplatz.",tip:"The bone chapel is small but genuinely moving. The Skywalk platform (no entry fee, included with the Salzbergbahn) gives the postcard view of the village from 600m above."},
      {time:"Wed 24 Jun · 16:00",icon:"🚂",title:"Hallstatt → Salzburg return",desc:"Last comfortable train back is ~17:00 from Hallstatt — earlier is safer. Reverse the route: ferry across, train to Attnang-Puchheim, change, train to Salzburg Hbf. Arrive ~19:00. Evening: dinner at Augustiner Bräustübl (monastery brewery since 1621) — fill your stein at the source.",tip:"The last train of the day departs Hallstatt around 19:00 — DO NOT miss it. The schedule thins out fast in the evening. Grab a coffee at the station before boarding."},
      {time:"Thu 25 Jun · 09:00",icon:"☕",title:"Morning Salzburg — Café Tomaselli",desc:"Café Tomaselli, Alter Markt 9 — founded 1705, oldest continuously operating café in Salzburg. Order Melange (Viennese coffee with cream, €4.50). Mozart's birthplace Getreidegasse 9 (€12pp, 45 min) if you want. The street itself is free and medieval.",tip:"Café Tomaselli has been serving coffee for 320 years. The waitresses in traditional dress, the painted ceiling, the marble tables — this is unchanged from the 18th century."},
      {time:"Thu 25 Jun · 13:30",icon:"🚄",title:"Railjet → Wien Hbf",desc:"OBB Railjet from Salzburg Hbf to Wien Hbf direct. 2h 25min, €9–35pp Sparschiene if booked early. Trains run every hour from Platforms 1–3. Arrive Wien Hbf ~16:00. The route runs through the Salzkammergut foothills along the Salzach valley.",tip:"Sparschiene fares are released ~3 months ahead and disappear quickly — €9 if early, €35 walk-up. The Bistro car serves Schnitzel wrap €6, coffee €3. Wien Hbf (NOT Westbahnhof or Meidling) — confirm on your ticket."},
    ],
