    story:"For 640 years the Habsburg dynasty ruled an empire from Vienna that at its peak stretched from Spain to Turkey and had 50 million subjects. They paid for everything — Mozart, Beethoven, Brahms, Schubert, Mahler all composed in Vienna. They built Schönbrunn Palace (1,441 rooms, 40 formal state rooms open to the public) as their summer residence. Gustav Klimt painted The Kiss in 1907–08 using real gold leaf — two figures wrapped in gold on a cliff edge. The painting has never left the Belvedere. The Vienna State Opera stages 50–60 different operas every season with the Vienna Philharmonic. Standing tickets cost €3.",
    history:"Celtic settlement on the Danube. Roman garrison Vindobona 15 BC. Habsburg capital from 1438. The Congress of Vienna (1814–15) redrew the map of Europe after Napoleon. Sigmund Freud developed psychoanalysis here. The Austro-Hungarian Empire collapsed in 1918. Vienna was occupied by the Soviet Union 1945–1955. Today it is Austria's capital with 1.9 million people.",
    itinerary:[
      {time:"Thu 25 Jun · 16:00",icon:"🚉",title:"Arrive Wien Hbf — afternoon check-in",desc:"Wien Hbf (Hauptbahnhof) is a modern station, U1 and U6 metro lines. Your Favoriten or Meidling Airbnb is 10–20 min by U-Bahn or 15 min walk. Drop bags then head straight to first Vienna café for late afternoon Melange.",tip:"Wien Hbf is NOT the same as Wien Westbahnhof or Wien Meidling. Your Railjet from Salzburg arrives at Wien Hbf specifically. Buy a 24-hour Vienna pass (€8pp) at the U-Bahn machine."},
      {time:"Fri 26 Jun · 09:00",icon:"🏰",title:"Schönbrunn Palace + Gloriette",desc:"Hietzing U4 metro, 20 min from centre. The gardens are FREE to walk — they are extraordinary even without entering the palace (1,441 rooms, Grand Tour €25pp). Walk to the Gloriette (free) at the top of the gardens for the best panoramic view of Vienna — the palace, the city, the hills beyond.",tip:"The gardens take 1.5 hrs to walk properly. Go at 09:00 before tour groups. The Neptune Fountain at the base of the hill is spectacular."},
      {time:"12:00",icon:"🛒",title:"Naschmarkt + lunch",desc:"U4 to Kettenbrückengasse. Vienna's main outdoor market — Mon–Sat, closes 18:00. Turkish, Middle Eastern, Austrian, Italian stalls. Lunch €6–8pp. The most international food experience in Austria. The Saturday flea market section at the south end is worth browsing.",tip:"Falafel + hummus from any of the Middle Eastern stalls is CHF 6 and excellent. Much better value than sit-down restaurants nearby."},
      {time:"14:00",icon:"🎨",title:"⭐ Belvedere Palace — Klimt's The Kiss",desc:"Book at belvedere.at — €16pp. The most famous painting in Austria, possibly in Central Europe. 180cm × 180cm gold leaf, 1907–08. Klimt used real gold leaf over oil paint. The couple stand on a cliff edge covered in a golden garment — nobody knows who they are. The Upper Belvedere palace is itself one of the most beautiful baroque buildings in Vienna.",tip:"The painting hangs in a dedicated room. The Zuckerkandl exhibition nearby (same ticket) gives context about Vienna's artistic scene — Schiele, Klimt, Kokoschka together."},
      {time:"17:00",icon:"🎭",title:"Vienna State Opera — €3 standing tickets",desc:"Box office opens exactly 80 min before each performance. Queue starts forming 2 hrs before. €3 standing room — the Vienna Philharmonic, the same singers, the same hall as a €200 seat. Check the programme at wiener-staatsoper.at 2 weeks before your visit.",tip:"Standing room is at the back of the stalls and in the upper galleries. The acoustics in this hall are extraordinary from anywhere. Dress is smart casual — no shorts."},
      {time:"Sat 27 Jun · 09:00",icon:"🚂",title:"Regiojet → Prague direct",desc:"4hrs. €15–25pp. FREE coffee on board. Book at regiojet.com. Direct, no change. Arrive Praha hl.n. ~13:00.",tip:"Regiojet is always cheaper than OBB for Vienna→Prague. Free coffee is real — they come through with it. No seat reservation extra charge."},
    ],
